From 5d3af4273084e3189b28dbff938120011538d823 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:22:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DRMStereo: an EDID extension whose data blocks would end past
 it is not read

Byte 2 of a CTA-861 extension tells where its data blocks end. A value
above 127 points past the extension; it was cut to 127 and the extension
read. The kernel does not read such an extension
(cea_db_collection_size() in drm_edid.c), so a driver that lists 3D modes
lists none from it; it is not read here either.

Host test: drmstereo_test (also for an entry of a format that is not the
first of the EDID, and for an EDID with two HDMI vendor blocks, which had
no case).
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMStereo.h | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMStereo.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMStereo.h
index 8352e49..f9c12b3 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMStereo.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMStereo.h
@@ -584,8 +584,12 @@ inline Edid3D Parse(std::span<const uint8_t> edid)
     if (block[0] != 0x02 || block[1] < 3 || !sumsToZero(block))
       continue;
 
-    // the data blocks lie between byte 4 and the first detailed timing
-    const std::size_t end = std::min<std::size_t>(block[2], BLOCK - 1);
+    // The data blocks lie between byte 4 and the first detailed timing, whose place byte 2
+    // tells. Less than 4 says that there are none; a place past the checksum is no extension
+    // to read, and the kernel does not read such a one either.
+    if (block[2] < 4 || block[2] > BLOCK - 1)
+      continue;
+    const std::size_t end = block[2];
     for (std::size_t i = 4; i < end;)
     {
       const unsigned int tag = block[i] >> 5;
-- 
